"ideaIndexRules enforces:\n  - idea-index-completeness: spec/ideas/README.md lists every active idea;\n    spec/ideas/archived/README.md lists every archived idea.\n  - idea-index-row-sync: each row's Status, Date, Owner, and Promotes To\n    cells in spec/ideas/README.md mirror the corresponding Idea file.\n    Drift typically arises after `idea-sync-lint-strict` updates an\n    Idea's `**Status:**` (e.g., Specified → Implementing); the index\n    row, being derived state, must follow.\n  - idea-archived-index-chronological: archived entries ordered by Date asc.\n\nWhen fix is true, missing/misordered entries and drifted rows are\nregenerated by rewriting the entire ## Index section from parsed Idea\nfields."
"(specRoot string, discovered []idea.Discovered, parsed map[string]*idea.Idea, fix bool) ([]Violation, bool)"
